Package: openmux-install-menu
Version: 1.1.0
Architecture: all
Maintainer: OpenMux <support@openmux.io>
Homepage: https://github.com/OpenMux
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Depends: xz-utils, zstd, fdisk, rpi-eeprom
Description: OpenMux install medium boot menu (neutral utility)
 Plain-text install/rescue menu for the OpenMux USB install medium: install a
 target image to disk, program the internal serial number, a boot-order and
 bootloader sub-menu that shows the current BOOT_ORDER and both bootloader
 versions before writing (and refuses downgrades, frozen modules and
 unverifiable writes), run board tests, drop to a shell, reboot/power off, and
 toggle the stick's overlay root filesystem.
 .
 The menu is a neutral utility only; autologin, the root shell profile and any
 other factory boot behaviour are not part of this package - they are applied by
 the openmux-install-medium layer at build time.
 .
 Every Depends backs a feature that degrades to a warning when its tool is
 absent: xz-utils/zstd decompress the embedded images, fdisk provides the sfdisk
 regenerate_disk_ids() needs, and rpi-eeprom provides the rpi-eeprom-config /
 rpi-eeprom-update the boot-order sub-menu reads and writes the module
 bootloader with. They are declared rather than assumed.
